@ifnottex
@node Top
@top BOCL Common Lisp

@code{bocl} is a Common Lisp implementation built from a small C kernel plus a
runtime-loaded Lisp prelude.
@end ifnottex

@menu
* Overview::            What bocl is.
* Invocation::          Running bocl from the command line.
* Files::               Installed layout and start-up files.
* Debugger::            The minimal debugger.
* Further reading::     Manuals and specifications.
@end menu

@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@code{bocl} runs an interactive read-eval-print loop, and can load files and
evaluate forms given on the command line before optionally entering the REPL.
On start-up it loads its system Lisp files --- the prelude and its supporting
files (@file{cl-exports.lisp}, @file{bignum.lisp},
@file{bignum-integration.lisp}).

@node Invocation
@chapter Invocation

@example
bocl [options]
@end example

The most common options are summarized below; see @command{bocl(1)} for the
full list.

@table @option
@item -h, --help
Print a usage summary and exit.
@item -V, --version
Print @code{(LISP-IMPLEMENTATION-VERSION)} and exit.
@item -l, --load @var{file}
Load @var{file}.
@item -x, -e, --eval @var{form}
Evaluate @var{form} (quote it for the shell).
@item -p, --package @var{package}
Start in @var{package}.
@item -b, --batch
Exit on end of file on @code{*STANDARD-INPUT*}.
@item -n, -norc, --no-init
Do not load @file{~/.boclrc}.
@item --no-prelude
Bare kernel only --- do not load the prelude.
@item --on-error @var{action}
On an unhandled error reaching the top level, do @var{action}: one of
@code{debug}, @code{exit}, @code{abort}, @code{appease}.  @code{debug} enters
the minimal debugger.
@item -quit, --quit
Quit when argument processing is done (otherwise enter the REPL).
@end table

@node Files
@chapter Files

The default install prefix is @file{/opt/local}.

@table @file
@item @var{PREFIX}/bin/bocl
The executable.
@item @var{PREFIX}/libexec/bocl/
The system Lisp files loaded at start-up: @file{prelude.lisp},
@file{cl-exports.lisp}, @file{bignum.lisp}, @file{bignum-integration.lisp}.
@item @var{PREFIX}/lib/libbocl.*
The runtime library (static and shared) for embedding bocl in a C program.
@item @var{PREFIX}/include/bocl/
The C headers for embedding.
@item ~/.boclrc
Per-user init file (unless @option{--no-init}).
@end table

The environment variable @env{BOCL_PRELUDE}, if set to a readable path,
overrides the prelude search.

@node Debugger
@chapter The minimal debugger

When an unhandled @code{SERIOUS-CONDITION} reaches the top level under
@option{--on-error debug} (or via @code{INVOKE-DEBUGGER} / @code{BREAK}), bocl
enters a minimal debugger: it prints the condition, a backtrace and the
available restarts, then runs a read-eval-print loop.  Keyword commands
(@code{:backtrace}, @code{:restart}, @code{:continue}, @code{:abort},
@code{:quit}, @code{:help}) and bare restart numbers select actions; any other
form is evaluated as Lisp in the error's dynamic context.  The complete
specification is in @file{debugger-specifications.org}.

